  "worked_solution": "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ae2c8de966219eb473c42fa809bfde49b52c7c88efaf83fc7ab0d602d734e722.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e243f3fb7515d9858599775ce0391f85f1de237f08380e1ec3b7403b1ecdbf53.png)",
